\DOC LOCAL_JDOUBLE_TAC

\TYPE {LOCAL_JDOUBLE_TAC : int -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Discharges one inlined subroutine call inside an {eventually} goal, replacing
the pre-call machine-state assumptions by post-call ones together with a
summarising implication about the subroutine's result, and advancing the goal's
state variable by one step.

\DESCRIBE
The single {int} argument {n} is the index of the state variable in the goal:
the goal's final state term is advanced from that index to the next one, and
the newly added assumptions are stated about the new state. Applied to a goal
whose conclusion is an {eventually} predicate about a machine state and whose
assumptions include a full symbolic state description, it yields one subgoal
with the same {eventually} body:
{
   A ?- eventually ... s_n
   ================================  LOCAL_JDOUBLE_TAC n
   A' ?- eventually ... s_(n+1)
}
\noindent Here {A'} keeps the non-state assumptions of {A} unchanged (side
conditions, non-overlapping facts, arithmetic and earlier result summaries),
while the block of assumptions describing the state before the call — register
and memory reads at {s_n}, flag values, the accumulated {MAYCHANGE} relation,
and the program-counter/stack-pointer facts — is removed and replaced by
corresponding reads at {s_(n+1)}, a {MAYCHANGE} relation extended with the
frame clobbered by the call, program-counter and stack-pointer facts for the
return site, and a new universally quantified assumption relating the
subroutine's input to the memory contents it writes at {s_(n+1)}.

\COMMENTS
All observed traces show this single-subgoal transformation, on goals of the
above form.

\ENDDOC
